WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.332
Every Azure CLI command runs with an Azure
identity.

2
00:00:05.412 --> 00:00:12.551
That identity may be a signed-in user,
service principal, managed identity,

3
00:00:12.631 --> 00:00:20.099
workload identity, federated CI/CD
identity, or another automation identity.

4
00:00:20.179 --> 00:00:26.987
The identity and its role assignments
determine what the script can read,

5
00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:30.801
create, update, deploy, or administer.

6
00:00:30.881 --> 00:00:36.043
RBAC design is therefore central to Azure
CLI security.

7
00:00:36.123 --> 00:00:39.308
Permissions should match the job.

8
00:00:39.388 --> 00:00:44.659
A reporting script should not use a
deployment identity.

9
00:00:44.739 --> 00:00:51.988
A validation step should not need the same
permissions as a production change.

10
00:00:52.068 --> 00:00:59.975
A rollback workflow should not
automatically share broad owner-level permissions.

11
00:01:00.055 --> 00:01:06.864
Least privilege should consider tenant,
subscription, resource group,

12
00:01:06.944 --> 00:01:14.082
resource, role, action, condition where
available, environment, and time.

13
00:01:14.162 --> 00:01:19.214
Role assignment should be intentional and
auditable.

14
00:01:19.294 --> 00:01:26.323
Teams should know which identities are
used by which scripts, who owns them,

15
00:01:26.403 --> 00:01:31.345
what scope they have, and why that access
is required.

16
00:01:31.425 --> 00:01:37.794
Broad Owner or Contributor access may make
automation easy to start,

17
00:01:37.874 --> 00:01:42.926
but it makes mistakes and incidents harder
to contain.

18
00:01:43.006 --> 00:01:50.474
Narrower scopes and purpose-specific
identities make review and response much

19
00:01:50.554 --> 00:01:51.433
cleaner.

20
00:01:51.513 --> 00:01:54.368
Access review is ongoing work.

21
00:01:54.448 --> 00:02:00.488
Automation identities can outlive the
script that created them,

22
00:02:00.568 --> 00:02:07.267
and temporary exceptions can become
permanent if nobody revisits them.

23
00:02:07.347 --> 00:02:12.838
Secure Azure CLI automation includes
ownership, purpose,

24
00:02:12.918 --> 00:02:17.970
rotation or renewal expectations,
revocation steps,

25
00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:24.420
and periodic review of stale access and
overbroad role assignments.
